{"name":"Gentian","hex":"#9079ad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gentian","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various herbs of the family Gentianaceae found in temperate and mountainous regions with violet or blue flowers.","Dried roots and rhizome of European gentian (Gentiana lutea), used as a tonic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gentian"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gentiana","blocks":[{"text":"Gentiana is a genus of flowering plants belonging to the gentian family (Gentianaceae), the tribe Gentianeae, and the monophyletic subtribe Gentianinae. With over 300 species, it is considered a large genus. Gentians are notable for their mostly large trumpet-shaped flowers, which are often of an intense blue hue, though some are also bright yellow. The type species of the genus is Gentiana lutea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Gentiana-verna2.jpg/330px-Gentiana-verna2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gentiana","wikidata":"Q144682"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Gentiana_frigida-flowers.jpg/500px-Gentiana_frigida-flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Gentiana_frigida-flowers.jpg/500px-Gentiana_frigida-flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gentiana frigida","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGentiana_frigida-flowers.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/UGH998.jpg/500px-UGH998.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/UGH998.jpg/1280px-UGH998.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe